Factory Pattern is a creational pattern it decides which object to create, 
while Strategy Pattern is a behavioral pattern it decides how an operation should be performed.
Factory Pattern create objects while Strategy Pattern change behaviour
In Factory Pattern decision happens at object creation time while in Strtegy it happens at runtime
Factory Pattern is used when you want to create diff obj based on input without using new keyword
Strategy Pattern is used when you want to change behaviour at runtime without changing obj
Factory Pattern chooses which class to instantiate and return a new obj 
Stratgy pattern choose which algo to use
Real ex: 
 Factory Pattern – “What do you want?”
You go to a shop and say:

“Orange juice”
“Apple juice”

The shop creates and gives you the juice.
✅ You don’t care how it’s made
✅ You only choose the type of object
👉 Factory → creates the object

Strategy Pattern – “How do you want it prepared?”
You already asked for orange juice, but now you choose:

With sugar
Without sugar
With ice

The juice is same, but behavior/preparation changes.
👉 Strategy → changes behavior
